ame history is: Play B6, Chi B7, Play B2, Peng B5.\\nThe game history of the next player is: Play J2, Play B5.\\nThe game history of the player sitting across is: Play W8, Play F1.\\nThe game history of the previous player is: Play T2, Play B8.\\nThe followings are your valid actions:[Play W2; Play F1; Play B8; Play T7; Play B1; Play T2; Play F4]\\u3002\", \"reasoning\": \"\", \"output\": \"Evaluation: [The hand currently has a concealed pung of B5, a chow of B6-B7-B8, and a mix of suited and honor tiles. The hand is not yet close to a high-point pattern, so the priority is to build toward a structured hand while minimizing risk. The most useful tile to discard is W2, as it is a simple tile with no immediate value in the current hand and can be safely played without giving others an advantage.]\\nReason: [W2 is a simple tile that does not contribute to any current melds or potential patterns, and discarding it reduces the risk of giving others a chance to complete a chow or pung.]\\nAnswer: Play W2\"}"}
